      "location": "Bay St. Louis",
      "category": "Arts & Culture",
      "description": "Create a dazzling glass mosaic skull inspired by Halloween or D\u00eda de los Muertos in this fun, beginner-friendly art workshop led by mosaic artist Susan McManus.Get creative and celebrate the season while learning the art of mosaic design. In this hands-on class, participants will create a custom Halloween or Day of the Dead mosaic skull using colorful glass pieces in a variety of shapes, sizes, and textures. Whether you choose a vibrant sugar skull design or a classic bone-inspired look, you'll leave with a unique handmade decoration to enjoy year after year.With guidance from experienced mosaic artist Susan McManus, students will learn the fundamentals of mosaic art, including how to design, arrange, glue, and grout glass pieces to create a finished work of art. No previous mosaic experience is required, making this class perfect for beginners and creative enthusiasts alike.Event DetailsSupply Fee: $10 payable directly to the instructor on the day of classRegistration: Spaces are limited. Early registration is recommended.Register online: https://tinyurl.com/MosaicSkullWhat You'll LearnDuring this workshop, participants will:Design a Halloween or Day of the Dead-themed mosaic skullSelect and arrange colorful glass piecesLearn proper mosaic layout and composition techniquesSecure glass pieces using mosaic adhesivesDiscover the basics of grouting and finishing a mosaic projectComplete a beautiful handmade artwork to take homeMaterials IncludedAll materials are provided, including:Skull-shaped mosaic baseAssorted glass pieces in various colors, shapes, and sizesAdhesives and mosaic toolsGrout and finishing materialsIndividual work trays and suppliesStudents do not need to bring any materials.About the InstructorSusan McManus has been teaching glass mosaic art at Second Studio in Waveland for more than 10 years. Known for her welcoming teaching style, Susan enjoys helping students of all skill levels discover the joy of creating mosaics and leave with artwork they are proud to display.Whether you're looking for a creative Halloween activity, a unique D\u00eda de los Muertos art project, or an introduction to glass mosaics, this workshop offers a fun and rewarding experience. Join Susan McManus and create a sparkling mosaic skull that's as bold, colorful, and unique as you are!",
