      "location": "Gulfport/Biloxi",
      "category": "Dining",
      "description": "The Maritime & Seafood Industry Museum will be hosting the Opening Reception for From Longleaf to Low Tide - Mixed-Media Views of the Mississippi Gulf Coast by artist Suzanne Findeisen, on October 8, 5:30 p.m. to 7 pm. Admission to the opening reception is free, and light refreshments will be served. View the exhibit, meet the artist, and tour the museum!This exhibition celebrates the landscapes and living rhythms of the Mississippi Gulf Coast, from longleaf pines and bayous to fish, birds, shrimp, and the waterways that connect them.Using layers of hand-painted and found papers, acrylic paint, drawing, and collage, Suzanne Findeisen builds each work piece by piece. Fragments of paper, pattern, color, and texture remain visible beneath the surface, reflecting the layered nature of the coast itself.The work is rooted in observation, memory, and a lifelong connection to this region. Rather than simply depicting the Gulf Coast, these pieces explore its movement, resilience, color, and sense of place, inviting viewers to look again at the familiar landscapes and creatures that surround us.The exhibit will be open October 8 through December 31, 2026.",
