      "location": "Bay St. Louis",
      "category": "Dining",
      "description": "The 100 Men Hall will screen Sabbath Queen on Tuesday, October 13, 2026, at 7 p.m. Twenty-one years in the making, Sabbath Queen follows Amichai Lau-Lavie\u2019s journey from radical drag queen to influential Rabbi of a God-optional, artist-driven New York synagogue.Sabbath Queen received a New York Times Critic's Pick and was named as one of The New York Times favorite movies of the 21st century. The screening is free, and we appreciate your RSVP so we can ensure you have a seat.\u201cAwe-inspiring. Enthralling. Sabbath Queen is a rich and intimateportrait\u2026 One of the best films I\u2019ve seen this year.\" - The Hollywood Reporter\"Provocative.\" - Variety\"Shrewdly asks hard questions about what it means to be Jewish in the21st century.\" - IndieWireSandi DuBowski\u2019s epic documentary Sabbath Queen\u2014shot over the span of twenty-one years\u2014follows Amichai Lau-Lavie, an Israeli descended from an unbroken line of thirty-eight rabbis stretching back a thousand years. Sabbath Queen is witness to Lau-Lavie\u2019s unfailing courage and grace, as he grapples with key questions of who we are and who we will be. Stimulating and moving, DuBowski\u2019s film ends with Lau-Lavie\u2019s words on Israel and Palestine post-October 7th as he evokes the challenge of our lifetime: \u201cHow do we reimagine our sacred traditions to achieve peace?\u201dThe film has won 14 awards in US, UK, Poland, Norway, Switzerland and Germany - Zurich Film Festival Jury Special Mention, The Hamptons Film Festival Queer Sherzum Award, Woodstock Film Festival Story of Ha Change Maker Award, Ashland Film Festival Queer Award, Salem Film Festival Cultura Cuts Editing Award, Oslo Fusion Film Festival Best Documentary, Boston Jewish Film Festival Audience Award, UK Jewish Film Best Documentary, Warsaw Jewish Film Festival Best Documentary, The Polin Museum Gran Prix, Perlen Queer Film Festival Hannover Best Documentary, Florida Film Critics Best Documentary, Freiburg Gay Film Week, and SIMA Awards Special Mention.It is 100% on Rotten Tomatoes.Food for purchase from Caroline's Creole Cooking food truck, specializing in a wide array of Creole dishes.",
