      "description": "Step back in time during the 40th Annual Fall Muster at Beauvoir, one of the Mississippi Gulf Coast's most anticipated living history events! This immersive weekend experience invites visitors to explore the sights, sounds, and traditions of the 1860s while enjoying interactive demonstrations, historical reenactments, family activities, and Southern hospitality.Experience life in the 1860s through authentic camp life, period music, living historians, military and civilian reenactors, and hands-on educational programs. Guests can stroll through historic encampments, learn about daily life during the era, and enjoy special attractions, including the popular Ladies' Tea and Small Muster, a kid-friendly area featuring activities and demonstrations designed for young history enthusiasts.Weekend HighlightsBattle Reenactments at 2 p.m. on Saturday and SundayAuthentic military and civilian campsLiving history demonstrationsPeriod music and entertainmentLadies' Tea on SaturdaySmall Muster activities for childrenTurkey Shoot competitionsHistorical sutlers and specialty vendorsCamp social gatherings and live entertainmentFamily-friendly activities throughout the weekendFood, Vendors & ShoppingBrowse a variety of sutlers and vendors offering period-inspired merchandise, handcrafted goods, and unique souvenirs. Enjoy delicious festival favorites and snacks, including:Sausage dogsHamburgers and hot dogsBoiled peanutsNachosDesserts and sweet treatsEducational School DayThe Fall Muster traditionally hosts a special School Day on Friday for students in grades 4 and above. Public, private, and homeschool groups are encouraged to attend this engaging, hands-on learning experience.AdmissionAdults (18+): $20 Daily | $30 Weekend PassChildren (6-17): $7 Daily | $10 Weekend PassChildren 5 & Under: FreeWhether you're a history enthusiast, visiting the Mississippi Gulf Coast, or looking for a unique family outing, the Fall Muster at Beauvoir offers an unforgettable opportunity to experience history brought to life! With battle reenactments, historical demonstrations, sutlers, vendors, food, snacks, and fun for the entire family, this annual Biloxi event is a must-see fall tradition.",
