      "location": "Bay St. Louis",
      "category": "Festival",
      "description": "5th Annual Winter Solstice Lantern Parade & Beach BonfireThe Winter Solstice is the shortest day of the year, a turning point when the nights begin to shorten and light starts its return. For centuries, communities have marked this moment with fire, lanterns, and celebration. In Bay St. Louis, The Arts has created its own joyful ritual- illuminating the dark with a parade of lanterns, then gathering with neighbors to celebrate all winter holidays together5th Annual Winter Solstice Handmade Parade & Beach BonfireCelebrate the longest night of the year with us on December 21 at 5:30 PM!Gather at The Arts, Hancock County to join our walking parade to Washington Street, where a beach bonfire awaits. What to Bring:Any type of Lantern (battery-operated only, prefer handmade)Folding chair or blanket (drop off at the beach area prior to parade)Beverage of your choiceSnack to share if you likeAll are welcome! Bring your neighbors, and feel free to meet us directly at the bonfire if you prefer.Let\u2019s light up the night together!This is a family-friendly event. No dogs, please! Friends are always welcome!",
