      "date": "2027-03-20",
      "title": "Arts Alive! 2027",
      "location": "Bay St. Louis",
      "category": "Dining",
      "description": "Experience one of the Coast's most beloved arts celebrations at Arts Alive! 2027, Hancock County's premier arts festival! Join artists, makers, musicians, vendors, and art enthusiasts for a weekend filled with creativity, culture, live entertainment, and community in the heart of Bay St. Louis.Held throughout the Historic Depot Arts District along Blaize Avenue, Arts Alive! takes place on the newly renovated grounds surrounding the historic Bay St. Louis L&N Train Depot and the Mamie Hillery Arts Center, creating a vibrant setting for visitors to discover local and regional talent.Event DetailsDates: Saturday, March 20 & Sunday, March 21, 2027Time: 10 AM to 5 PM dailyAdmission: Open to the publicCelebrate Art, Music, Creativity & CommunityArts Alive! invites visitors to explore:Fine art and handcrafted works from local and regional artistsArtisan vendors and makersLive music and entertainmentInteractive creative experiencesFamily-friendly activitiesFood and refreshmentsThe thriving arts community of Bay St. LouisWhether you're an art collector, a casual browser, or simply looking for a fun weekend on the Mississippi Gulf Coast, Arts Alive! offers something for everyone.A Rich Arts TraditionFounded in 2004 as a studio tour featuring members of The Arts, Hancock County, Arts Alive! has grown from a small community event into one of South Mississippi's signature arts festivals.As the festival expanded over the years, it outgrew its original downtown footprint. Following the establishment of the Mamie Hillery Arts Center, made possible through the generous support of local art patron Mamie Hillery, The Arts, Hancock County found a permanent home in the heart of Bay St. Louis' Historic Depot District. Today, Arts Alive! proudly calls this thriving arts destination home, showcasing the creativity and culture that make Hancock County unique.Calling All Artists, Vendors & MakersApplications are now open for:Visual ArtistsArtisans & MakersCraft VendorsCreative BusinessesMakerSpace ParticipantsRegister now and save! Early registration discounts are available through August 31, 2027.Why Attend Arts Alive! 2027?Discover original artwork and handmade goodsMeet talented Coast artistsExplore Bay St. Louis' Historic Depot Arts DistrictEnjoy live music and cultural experiencesSupport local arts and creative entrepreneursExperience one of Mississippi's premier arts festivalsCome be a pART of it all at Arts Alive! 2027 in beautiful Bay St. Louis, Mississippi!",
      "url": "https://www.coastalmississippi.com/events/arts-alive-2027/",
